      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to use the given operation definition \\( a \\oplus b = 3a + 4b \\).\n\nHere's the specific task: Calculate \\( 3 \\oplus 1 \\).\n\nAccording to the operation definition, we substitute \\( a = 3 \\) and \\( b = 1 \\) into the expression \\( 3a + 4b \\).\n\nSo, let's compute \\( 3 \\oplus 1 \\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\oplus 1 = 3(3) + 4(1)\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate \\( 3 \\times 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 3 = 9\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( 4 \\times 1 \\):\n\n\\[\n4 \\times 1 = 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we add these results together:\n\n\\[\n9 + 4 = 13\n\\]\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n\\[\n3 \\oplus 1 = 13\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{13}\n\\]",
